    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.base16\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nHi echasnovski! Can different colors be set for @tag, @tag.attribute and @tag.delimiter for HTML in mini.base16.\r\nCurrently HTML looks something like below with no differentiation between tag, attribute and delimiter.\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0a4193ec-898d-43ee-a2b1-dc4e03439411)\r\n",
